// CLIFF.QS0 - a Clifford-only circuit for the stabilizer engine.
//
// Demonstrates: the stabilizer engine (--stabilizer), Clifford gates
// (H, S, CNOT, CZ), and exact simulation.
//
// Qubit-level explanation:
//   All gates here are Clifford gates: they conjugate Pauli operators to
//   Pauli operators. Such circuits can be simulated exactly, and in
//   polynomial time, by the stabilizer engine, which tracks the n-qubit
//   stabilizer group instead of the 2^n amplitudes. Plasma selects the
//   engine automatically with --stabilizer, and the results are identical
//   to the statevector reference for the same seed.
//
//   The circuit builds a three-qubit GHZ state and adds relative phases:
//     H 0; CNOT 0 1; CNOT 1 2   give (|000>+|111>)/sqrt2,
//     S 2 adds a phase to the |1> component of qubit 2,
//     CZ 1 2 negates the amplitude when qubits 1 and 2 are both |1>.
//   The phases do not affect the probabilities, so the measured distribution
//   is still the 50/50 |000>/|111> split.
//
// Run:
//   plasma run examples/CLIFF.QS0 --stabilizer --shots 1000
//   plasma run examples/CLIFF.QS0 --shots 1000              (reference)
QUBITS 3
H 0
CNOT 0 1
CNOT 1 2
S 2
CZ 1 2
SHOT 1000
PRINT
END